# {{id}}

A cox plugin scaffolded by `cox plugin new {{id}} --lang kotlin`. `docs/design/plugins.md`
(PL) and `docs/plugins.md` in the [cox repository](https://github.com/pyrlyn/cox)
have the full contract; this file only covers this package.

Capabilities asked for at scaffold time: {{with_summary}}. Edit `plugin.toml`'s
`[capabilities]` to change them, and `src/wasmWasiMain/kotlin/Main.kt` for the
exports that back them.

## Build

The cox Kotlin PDK is not published yet, so the build takes it from a cox
checkout: set `coxSdk` in `gradle.properties` to its `plugins/sdk-kotlin`.

```
mise use java gradle   # once, or install a JDK and Gradle yourself
just build
```

compiles the Kotlin/Wasm (`wasmWasi`) module and stages `plugin.toml` with
`{{crate_name}}.wasm` in `build/plugin`. `plugin.toml` has `wasi = true` because
Kotlin's stdlib imports WASI's `random_get`.

## Try it

```
just smoke
```

builds the package, installs it into a scratch `COX_HOME` with
`cox plugin install --yes` and checks that `cox plugin list --json` reports it
`loaded`. `cox` must be on `PATH`.

## Install for real

```
cox plugin install build/plugin --yes
```
